"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T17:36:32-08:00","id":1503867,"title":"","content":"I noticed the sections for Notable Vault and Actual Plays, which count as types of fan-made content. Could you please include my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eM6TJ-gB0i6FZFL2OXWNaoijDCZW7-Ry7_U-kNtK6X0/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><b>God-Machine version of Genius: The Transgression?</b></a> Below is the explanation for why I think it should be included in the original post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This version of Genius 2ed explores an alternate interpretation of Genii. Unlike the standard version written by Moochava and updated by The King's Raven, these Genii are mortals who have been fundamentally altered by delving too deep into the secret laws of reality known as occult-physics, which are described in Demon: The Descent, along with its various supplements. These Genii are effectively a variation of the Stigmatic Template, but with several important changes, mainly the capacity to use the Gadget Installation System that is normally available only to Demons according to the rules-as-written.<br /> <br /> The central purpose of this homebrew is to adapt the standard version of Genius into the setting of Demon: The Descent, which is useful for STs who do not want to introduce an entire cosmology from a fansplat into their Chronicle. It is also useful for players who want to play mad scientists, but do not want to use the mechanics of the standard version of Genius. All the important and iconic features are still present, such as Catalysts, Foundations, Fellowships, Havoc, Jabir, Diatribes, Unmada, Manes, Bardos, Orphans and Clockstoppers. You are not obligated to use the entirety of the default setting for Demon: The Descent or Genius: The Transgression when playing as these God-Machine Genii, you can adjust the details to suit your Chronicle. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T09:53:25-08:00","id":1503899,"title":"","content":"Lemme think on it. I've included Vault stuff because it is kinda semi-official and I'm not including everything. I'm also a bit reluctant to include stuff from the fan lines on the lists and I'm very much not a fan of Genius in particular. That said though, the bit you've quoted does look interesting, so I'll take a look when I have a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>P